WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.360
I'm Russ Michaels with Tercet Law.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.320
I want to tell you what actually happens in Texas when someone dies without

3
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:11.760
a plan.

4
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.000
Not to scare you, just so you know.

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.280
Without a will, Texas law decides who inherits.

6
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:24.360
It follows a formula written by the legislature, and that formula may not

7
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.780
match the people that you choose.

8
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.720
If your children are young and neither parent is there to raise them, a

9
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.140
judge decides who will.

10
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.220
And your family will often have to go to court before they can sell the

11
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.640
house or settle your accounts.

12
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.260
That takes time and money, at the hardest moment of their lives.

13
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.220
None of that's anyone's fault.

14
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.940
It's just what happens by default.

15
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.880
A plan changes the default.

16
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.060
A will that names who inherits and who raises your kids.

17
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.260
A trust when it fits to keep things private and out of court.

18
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.800
Powers of attorney so someone you trust can act for you if you can't.

19
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.760
It doesn't have to be complicated.

20
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.080
It just has to be done.

21
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.640
There's a door here for you.

22
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.760
So click the link below and let's put on paper what you've been putting

23
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.060
off.

